b.com/users/enginsoysal/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enginsoysal/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enginsoysal/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enginsoysal/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enginsoysal/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enginsoysal/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enginsoysal/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"content_type":"text/plain; charset=utf-8","state":"uploaded","size":1839,"digest":"sha256:092ebda967f9fa5f75fa7805fd86625ffefc1ce6ed74be5cac1eef9aad0f6d1f","download_count":0,"created_at":"2026-11-18T03:03:39Z","updated_at":"2026-11-18T03:03:39Z","browser_download_url":"https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/releases/download/m134-v0.13.4/M13STAGE4-SHA256SUMS.txt"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enginsoysal/engacer-os/releases/assets/761647880","id":761647880,"node_id":"RA_kwDOVj6ISs4tZdMI","name":"m13stage4-starter-manifest.json","label":"","uploader":{"login":"enginsoysal","id":103884748,"node_id":"U_kgDOBjEnzA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/103884748?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/enginsoysal","html_url":"https://github.com/enginsoysal","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enginsoysal/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enginsoysal/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enginsoysal/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enginsoysal/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enginsoysal/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enginsoysal/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enginsoysal/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enginsoysal/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enginsoysal/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"content_type":"application/json","state":"uploaded","size":653,"digest":"sha256:a06ff56de45576261e7790037e9f978516e4d90debcb4dfe333587828c41c0e7","download_count":0,"created_at":"2026-11-18T03:03:39Z","updated_at":"2026-11-18T03:03:39Z","browser_download_url":"https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/releases/download/m134-v0.13.4/m13stage4-starter-manifest.json"}],"tarball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enginsoysal/engacer-os/tarball/m134-v0.13.4","zipball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enginsoysal/engacer-os/zipball/m134-v0.13.4","body":"# Engacer OS M13.4 / 0.13.4 - Installation and installed startup\n\nNative qualification passes M13-STAGE4-VM-v1. This scoped release finishes the progress, completion, failure and recovery journey and requalifies actual installed startup. Use the matching [installation and recovery guide](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/21d6bc100e87a95fd01573dff9346c444d551614/docs/handbook/install-m134.md). M13.5-M13.12 remain separate ordered deliveries.\n\nBuild: `8764f1439e79ea937d27ac5e268697eb`.\nISO SHA256: `2f18d630cc695cbd1218b14d47ef34d4ada238bf32ad06daef845a03c44d0fb5`.\nVMware ZIP SHA256: `7df4d7178f6ee76dfdff2beeb1d16a903dd228439adf474809715f57b1b58599`.\n\n## Native changes\n\nInstallation, verified completion and recovery share the native typography, controls and compositor. Progress names actual backend work, with no invented time estimate or forced delay. Identical progress notifications skip redundant repaint while retaining storage verification, audio servicing and serial observations. Completion identifies the saved local account and the real restart into the installed desktop.\n\nA failed operation never claims success. Live recovery exposes supported boot maintenance with disk selection and review. A failed installed startup without the matching ISO explains what to attach and offers restart and diagnostics; unavailable boot maintenance is hidden. Restart is a real firmware reset, not a promise to repair arbitrary damaged user data.\n\nCapacity formatting uses the actual sector width. A 4096-byte-sector NVMe disk displays its correct 2-GiB capacity and remains inspection-only for installation; its complete bytes remain unchanged.\n\n## Exact native qualification\n\n[Acceptance](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/21d6bc100e87a95fd01573dff9346c444d551614/evidence/M13/4/acceptance-results.json), [resources](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/21d6bc100e87a95fd01573dff9346c444d551614/evidence/M13/4/resources.json) and [visual review](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/21d6bc100e87a95fd01573dff9346c444d551614/evidence/M13/4/visual-review.json) bind 602 compiled inputs and the exact media. Fourteen fresh enabled-device VMware profiles cover SATA, IDE, LSI Logic, LSI SAS, PVSCSI and NVMe with BIOS and UEFI, BusLogic with BIOS, and the exact SATA/UEFI starter. Each performs real installation, retained-ISO startup, persistent graphical folder creation and two disk-only starts without a forced firmware boot order. The starter also verifies the supported original 7-Zip console MSI lifecycle and 106 payload hashes.\n\nFive reference display/control/install profiles cover 1024x768, 1280x800, 1920x1080, 1920x1200 at 150% and physical 3840x2160 at 200%. Separate progress/recovery frames include the minimum 800x600 setup. A 25% busy installation capture independently confirms changed disk bytes; verified completion follows. Fault tests verify explicit erasure consent, an unchanged separate disk, safe write failure, fresh retry after power-cycle and removing the external fault, boot-slot repair followed by real disk-only startup, and truthful failure after deliberately corrupting owned data-volume metadata.\n\nInitial harness navigation/map and resource-counter attempts are retained as diagnostics; they are not passing qualification. QEMU PVSCSI remains separately unqualified. Actual VMware PVSCSI results do not change that emulator limitation. Agent visual/scenario review is separate from a real human novice study.\n\n## Resource measurements and limits\n\nThe measured installation emits 96 backend progress notifications and 66 visible frame events, with no additional full outer-frame repaint. Content transitions are counted separately. Fixed installer state is 48,412 bytes, 16 bytes above M13.3; desktop fixed state stays 553,452 bytes and immutable fonts stay 251,248 bytes. Five display tasks retain zero managed pages and show stable idle halt on both virtual CPUs. Configured guest RAM, framebuffer storage and managed current/peak pages are separate categories.\n\nInstallation uses the whole selected disk and fresh explicit replacement consent. Resizing, filesystem conversion and data-preserving dual boot are unavailable. Quick format, delete and clear are not secure erasure. Boot-slot repair cannot recover arbitrary damaged personal files. Development media require Secure Boot off. Universal/physical hardware, vendor GPU 3D, Steam and general DOS/Windows compatibility remain outside this stage.\n"}